</code></pre> <p>This function, as noted, can be implemented in a user file when the callback is needed. It checks if the network link is up using <code>netif_is_link_up(netif)</code> and then controls the state of two LEDs using <code>HAL_GPIO_WritePin</code>. If the link is up, it turns on the green LED and turns off the red LED, and vice versa if the link is down.</p> <pre><code>ethernetif_notify_conn_changed(&amp;gnetif);
</code></pre> <p>This line calls the <code>ethernetif_notify_conn_changed</code> function and passes the <code>gnetif</code> structure as an argument.</p> lwip.c<pre><code>ethernetif_set_link(&amp;gnetif);
