    netif_set_up(&amp;gnetif);
    dhcp_start(&amp;gnetif);
}
</code></pre> <p>In this part of the code from the <code>lwip.c</code> file, it first sets the link status using <code>ethernetif_set_link(&amp;gnetif)</code>. Then, it checks if the link is up and the network interface is not up. If both conditions are met, it sets the network interface up and starts DHCP.</p>

